<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-Access">Access</h1>
<p>Production Airflow is hosted in our AWS account here:</p>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://af197965-ed5f-46f1-9853-f8f5f=
2bc332b.c30.us-west-2.airflow.amazonaws.com/home" rel=3D"nofollow">https://=
af197965-ed5f-46f1-9853-f8f5f2bc332b.c30.us-west-2.airflow.amazonaws.com/ho=
me</a></p>
<p></p>
<p>It uses AWS SSO, so first you need to log into AWS. You can also access =
Airflow via the AWS Console. Go to =E2=80=9CManaged Apache Airflow=E2=80=9D=
 then =E2=80=9COpen Airflow UI=E2=80=9D for the prod environment.</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> The above URL was generated by AWS. There is also=
 a vanity URL at <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://airflow.seesaw.=
me/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://airflow.seesaw.me</a>, but has some certifica=
te issues and needs some more work ( <span class=3D"confluence-jim-macro ji=
ra-issue" data-jira-key=3D"PLAT-918" data-client-id=3D"SINGLE_e237ef9d-8dd2=
-34de-8588-bf3b81a18d6a_88473854_712020:3aa06253-1b05-42a2-b9b6-a95af2383e2=
1"> <a href=3D"https://seesawhq.atlassian.net/browse/PLAT-918" class=3D"jir=
a-issue-key"><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-wait issue-placeholder"></spa=
n>PLAT-918</a> - <span class=3D"summary">Getting issue details...</span> <s=
pan class=3D"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-default issue-place=
holder">STATUS</span> </span> ).</p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-DevelopmentandTesting">Development and Te=
sting</h1>
<p></p>
<p>For development and testing, we can use <a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://github.com/aws/aws-mwaa-local-runner" rel=3D"nofollow"><span da=
ta-colorid=3D"z3webe8dc8"><u>aws-mwaa-local-runner</u></span></a>, a comman=
d line interface (CLI) utility that replicates an Amazon Managed Workflows =
for Apache Airflow (MWAA) environment locally.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>For quick Python test and debug runs of your DAG: </strong>try d=
ag.test() instead of the Docker container. <a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://airflow.apache.org/docs/apache-airflow/2.8.1/core-concepts/exec=
utor/debug.html#testing-dags-with-dag-test" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-col=
orid=3D"wvers7v51a"><u>See documentation</u></span></a></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_pay0147c2d8dSetup"><span class=3D"conflu=
ence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_pay0147c2d8d"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_pay0147c2d8d"></span></span>Setup</h1>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_9mvfn6uh6p6yMac/Linux(Ubuntu)"><span cla=
ss=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_9mvfn6uh6p6y">=
<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_9mvfn6uh6p6y"></span></span>M=
ac / Linux (Ubuntu)</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_7umb9rpuzd6jPrerequisites"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_7umb9rpuzd6j"><s=
pan class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_7umb9rpuzd6j"></span></span><br=
>
Prerequisites</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Install docker-compose and docker</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Colima, an open-source equivalent, works too. You may have it set up if =
you did the Seesaw Devbox Setup.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>sudo docker run hello-world (confirm docker installed successfully)</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Run which docker-compose to confirm docker-compose is installed as well.=
 If not then use your package manager (i.e. homebrew) to install.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-gu=
ide/key-pair-auth#configuring-key-pair-authentication" rel=3D"nofollow"><sp=
an data-colorid=3D"oizpddm6mq"><u>Set up a Snowflake key</u></span></a></p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>clone <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://github.com/shadowpuppet=
/dart" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-colorid=3D"y8a405xbsd"><u>dart</u></span=
></a> repo</p></li>
<li>
<p>Change to dart directory and run:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>git submodule init</p></li>
<li>
<p>git submodule update --init --recursive</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>Make files &amp; files/keys directory in your system outside of dart rep=
o. It will be used for connections, variables, private keys, etc. needed by=
 Airflow.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Keep variables &amp; connections json file in files directory.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Add your Snowflake private key to the files/keys directory and add =E2=
=80=9C./files/keys=E2=80=9D as a prefix.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"be1be769-adff-415f-86d=
5-8c6df53d5098">The file should now look something like this</span>:</p></l=
i>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "snowflake_conn_serviceaccount": {
    "conn_type": "snowflake",
    "login": "BOB",
    "password": "this-is-my-Snowflake-key-passphrase",
    "extra": {
      "account": "ISOHUKY-RHB81012",
      "role": "DEV_AIRFLOW",
      "database": "YOURTESTDB",
      "private_key_file": "./files/keys/snowflake.p8",
      "warehouse": "DEV_AIRFLOW_WH"
    }
  }
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Add export AIRFLOW_LOCAL_CONNECTIONS_DIR=3D&lt;path of files directory y=
ou just created&gt; to your shell initialization. (For example, add it to ~=
/.zshrc if you are using a Mac or Linux running Z Shell.)</p></li>
<li>
<p>[Optional] If you need to connect to the test Postgres DB for dashboard =
data, see <a href=3D"https://seesawhq.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/8=
8473854/Airflow+Development+Guide#_r5o83hp9u4vb" rel=3D"nofollow"><span dat=
a-colorid=3D"dh7h3i7wa8"><u>RDS Postgres Connection</u></span></a> below.</=
p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_3sl2l1qbcj88AddTestConnectionandVariable=
s"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_3s=
l2l1qbcj88"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_3sl2l1qbcj88"></s=
pan></span>Add Test Connection and Variables</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-TestConnections">Test Connections</h4>
<p>For each connection needed (like Snowflake), do the following in the dir=
ectory created outside of the dart repo:</p>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Make a copy of example connection file (airflow/aws-mwaa-local-runner/ex=
ample_connections/example_snowflake_connections.json) and call it connectio=
ns.json</p></li>
<li>
<p>Set account to ISOHUKY-RHB81012</p></li>
<li>
<p>Fill in the username and password values for your Snowflake user. Note t=
hat the password is the passphrase for your Snowflake key.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Fill in the filename for the private_key_file value with the key filenam=
e set up in the Prerequisites.</p></li>
</ol>
<h4 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-TestVariables">Test Variables</h4>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"d60aaba0-cf01-425b-9c2=
a-a15e7b2e346e">Create a file </span><code><span class=3D"inline-comment-ma=
rker" data-ref=3D"d60aaba0-cf01-425b-9c2a-a15e7b2e346e">variables.json</spa=
n></code><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"d60aaba0-cf01-42=
5b-9c2a-a15e7b2e346e"> in the same directory. Add the following:</span></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
    "SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE": "DEV_DB",
    "METRICS_FILE_FORMAT": "METRIC_FILE_FORMAT",
    "DEV_SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE": "DEV_DB",
    "METRICS_SNOWFLAKE_STAGE": "DATA_PLATFORM_DASHBOARD_STAGE",
    "METRICS_S3_REGION": "us-west-2"
  }</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_9kfbk5b1t1orStartEnvironment"><span clas=
s=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_9kfbk5b1t1or"><=
span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_9kfbk5b1t1or"></span></span>St=
art Environment</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>start docker or colima service</p></li>
<li>
<p>cd dart</p></li>
<li>
<p>git submodule update --init --recursive</p></li>
<li>
<p>cd airflow/aws-mwaa-local-runner/</p></li>
<li>
<p>[If running for the first time or if you have made changes to the Airflo=
w Docker container]: run <code>./mwaa-local-env build-image</code></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>If fails on chmod command step try: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"h=
ttps://github.com/aws/aws-mwaa-local-runner/issues/96#issuecomment-10436717=
48" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-colorid=3D"hjepi73dc7"><u>Link</u></span></=
a></p></li>
<li>
<p>If fails with Resolving www.python.org (www.python.org)... failed, try d=
ocker system prune</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"7fdf91ae-6856-4ba8-ba1=
0-a25d70d42a34">Run </span><code>./mwaa-local-env start</code> to start Air=
flow without <a href=3D"https://seesawhq.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/page=
s/88473854#_r5o83hp9u4vb" rel=3D"nofollow">RDS Postgres Connection</a>.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>This will also sync the files from your <code>dart/airflow/dags</code> t=
o the local runner so they will be used by the Docker container.</p></li>
<li>
<p>This will start a <strong>local Postgres container</strong> used by the =
Airflow local runner</p></li>
<li>
<p>Make sure VPN is off, if any.</p></li>
<li>
<p>This mode does not connect to the RDS proxy =E2=80=94 it uses the local =
Postgres instance for Airflow metadata.</p></li>
<li>
<p>To run with RDS proxy, use <code>./mwaa-local-env start --connect-to-rds=
-proxy</code></p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>After startup (should take 15-30 seconds), go to Airflow UI at <a class=
=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://localhost:8080" rel=3D"nofollow"><span da=
ta-colorid=3D"p3an8nsagp"><u>http://localhost:8080</u></span></a></p></li>
<li>
<p>Login if needed. Creds are username: admin, password: test</p></li>
<li>
<p>Press Ctrl+c to stop Airflow</p></li>
<li>
<p>If you want to add any dependency add it in requirements.txt. Or if you =
want to pull from s3 bucket then update S3_REQUIREMENTS_PATH=3D"" in .env.l=
ocalrunner file.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-DevelopmentEnvironment">Development Envir=
onment</h3>
<p>We recommend using <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://code.visua=
lstudio.com/" rel=3D"nofollow">Visual Studio Code</a> for writing Python an=
d SQL, with the following extensions:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-gu=
ide/vscode-ext" rel=3D"nofollow">Snowflake</a></p></li>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/=
items?itemName=3Dnjpwerner.autodocstring" rel=3D"nofollow">autoDocstring</a=
></p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_r5o83hp9u4vbRDSPostgresConnection"><span=
 class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_r5o83hp9u4=
vb"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_r5o83hp9u4vb"></span></sp=
an>RDS Postgres Connection</h3>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"8abf5588-98a1-4823-815=
b-827b58ad4099">There are multiple long lived environment that are run usin=
g RDS postgres : </span></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"bf=
b4edb5-aaf2-4157-8c5e-4edaa42360a0" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Environment</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>DB Instance</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Schema</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>prod</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>prod-seesaw-db</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>sessawprod</code></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>latest</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>test-seesaw-db</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>seesaw</code></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>beta</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>test-seesaw-db</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>beta</code></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>test</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>test-seesaw-db</code></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><code>testseesawdataplatform</code></p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p><strong>Any Data Platform development or testing should happen in the =
=E2=80=9Ctest=E2=80=9D environment. </strong>latest and beta is used by the=
 dashboard app and we shouldn=E2=80=99t make any data adjustments there wit=
hout notifying those teams.</p>
<p>To connect:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Ensure your IP address is allowed to access the SSH tunnel for the RDS i=
nstances. See <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassi=
an.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/88473854/Airflow+Development+Guide#[inlineExte=
nsion]How-to-Connect-to-Dashboard-RDS-Database" rel=3D"nofollow">here</a> f=
or instructions.</p></li>
<li>
<p>=E2=80=9CLook for =E2=80=9CEC2 - RDS Proxy Dev SSH Key=E2=80=9D in share=
d 1Password and save =E2=80=9Cprivate key=E2=80=9D value to a file called <=
code>ssh_host.pem</code>. Give sufficient permission(755) so that Airflow w=
ill be able to read it.</p></li>
<li>
<p><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/wiki=
/spaces/ENG/pages/edit-v2/88473854#%5BinlineExtension%5DAdd-Connection" rel=
=3D"nofollow">In the directory created</a> for storing airflow connections.=
 Add the downloaded <code>ssh_host.pem</code> file to the files/keys direct=
ory.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Add the following to the <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://sees=
aw-eng.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/edit-v2/88473854#%5BinlineExtens=
ion%5DAdd-Connection" rel=3D"nofollow">variables json</a> file</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">    "SS=
H_ADDRESS": "ec2-user@ec2-52-40-44-6.us-west-2.compute.amazonaws.com",
    "RDS_HOST": "test-seesaw-db-proxy.proxy-ceu8xezttjlx.us-west-2.rds.amaz=
onaws.com",
    "RDS_USER": "gcsqltestrwdataplatform",
    "RDS_SCHEMA": "testseesawdataplatform"</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>aws configure sso</p></li>
<li>
<p>export AWS_PROFILE=3Dprofile_name</p></li>
<li>
<p>export AIRFLOW_LOCAL_CONNECTIONS_DIR=3D&lt;path of files directory&gt;</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>./mwaa-local-env start --connect-to-rds-proxy</p></li>
<li>
<p>Once UI is up run dag with dag_id=3DPOSTGRESS_CONNECTION_TESTING. Both t=
ask should execute successfully</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Under the hood, an SSH tunnel is set up via local runner=E2=80=99s start=
 up script and environment variables are copied over to the local runner en=
vironment. One of these variables is <code>AIRFLOW_CONN_TEST_POSTGRES_IAM_C=
ONN</code>, which make a connection classed <code>test_postgres_iam_conn</c=
ode> available. It set the the <code>RDS_PASSWORD</code> value to the passw=
ord attribute of the connection. This means that the password will expire, =
which will require you to re-generate the password periodically and then re=
start local runner.<br></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_6o1fhf2loa8gTesting"><span class=3D"conf=
luence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_6o1fhf2loa8g"><span clas=
s=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_6o1fhf2loa8g"></span></span>Testing</h1=
>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_1yi6srue9wqInstallAct"><span class=3D"co=
nfluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_1yi6srue9wq"><span cla=
ss=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_1yi6srue9wq"></span></span>Install Act=
</h2>
<p><strong>Prerequisite: </strong>docker or colima</p>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-Ubuntu">Ubuntu</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>wget -qO act.tar.gz <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://github.co=
m/nektos/act/releases/latest/download/act_Linux_x86_64.tar.gz" rel=3D"nofol=
low"><u>https://github.com/nektos/act/releases/latest/download/act_Linux_x8=
6_64.tar.gz</u></a></p></li>
<li>
<p>sudo tar xf act.tar.gz -C /usr/local/bin act</p></li>
<li>
<p>rm -rf act.tar.gz</p></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"></p>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-Mac">Mac</h3>
<p>Try Homebrew: <code>brew install act</code></p>
<p>Alternatively, use one of these methods: <a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://nektosact.com/installation/index.html" rel=3D"nofollow"><span d=
ata-colorid=3D"e6p44hvi16"><u>https://nektosact.com/installation/index.html=
</u></span></a></p>
<p>Test to see if it works: <code>act --version</code></p>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_hgb91wuqpldeTestingwhilepushingyourcode"=
><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_hgb9=
1wuqplde"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_hgb91wuqplde"></spa=
n></span>Testing while pushing your code</h2>
<p>Prerequisite: <a href=3D"https://seesawhq.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/=
pages/88473854/Airflow+Development+Guide#_1yi6srue9wq" rel=3D"nofollow"><sp=
an data-colorid=3D"bojawhmu4e"><u>Install Act</u></span></a> and start dock=
er or colima.</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Set new pre-push path in your local by running <span data-colorid=3D"x9v=
zcvja74">git</span> <span data-colorid=3D"lckh0pwg3j">config</span> <span d=
ata-colorid=3D"vjxangral9">core.hooksPath</span> <span data-colorid=3D"z9d5=
lde45r">hooks</span> from <span data-colorid=3D"v4uqbjamfv">dart</span> dir=
ectory.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Once set whenever you do git push, your changes will be verified. If all=
 checks pass then only your code will be pushed.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_ndqczu17bpafHowtoManuallyRunTestsandLint=
Checks"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuid=
e-_ndqczu17bpaf"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_ndqczu17bpaf=
"></span></span>How to Manually Run Tests and Lint Checks</h2>
<p>These are the same tests and lint checks that run in GitHub when a PR br=
anch is pushed.</p>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Start docker or colima</p></li>
<li>
<p>Go to root of dart repo</p></li>
<li>
<p><a href=3D"https://seesawhq.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/88473854=
/Airflow+Development+Guide#_1yi6srue9wq" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-colori=
d=3D"ul5cfgu4c8"><u>Install =E2=80=98act=E2=80=99 if you haven=E2=80=99t al=
ready done so.</u></span></a></p></li>
<li>
<p>Run act and look for success (=F0=9F=8F=81 Job succeeded) or failures fr=
om each job</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>If on a Mac, you may need to run act -P ubuntu-latest=3D<a class=3D"exte=
rnal-link" href=3D"http://ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04" rel=3D"nof=
ollow"><span data-colorid=3D"he0xcgn82b"><u>ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act=
-22.04</u></span></a></p></li>
<li>
<p>This runs all the GitHub Action jobs in parallel, which results in their=
 output lines getting mixed together. You may find it easier to run the job=
s individually:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Run act -l to list all jobs</p></li>
<li>
<p>Run act =E2=80=93job &lt;job_name_from_prev_command&gt;</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Run =E2=80=98on github action: push=E2=80=99:</strong></p>
<p>There is a pre-push file attached that needs to be installed in the loca=
l system.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Link to pre-push file in ticket reference: <a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/browse/BEEH-103" rel=3D"nofollow"><s=
pan data-colorid=3D"no2ck3ogji"><u>https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/browse/=
BEEH-103</u></span></a></p>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Install it in your system. Steps in case missed can be referred over the=
 internet.</p></li>
<li>
<p>You will see results for this move only when there are sql changed files=
 which are run over in the pre-push file.</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_8uzt846pfn42HowtoaddConnectionsorVariabl=
es"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_8=
uzt846pfn42"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_8uzt846pfn42"></=
span></span><strong>How to add Connections or Variables</strong></h1>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_jodp34zi1w5hProd"><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_jodp34zi1w5h"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_jodp34zi1w5h"></span></span>Prod</h2>
<p>In MWAA, because it is within AWS, we can use the AWS Secrets Manager as=
 an alternative backend rather than the standard Airflow backend. That is w=
here most (if not all) of our Airflow variables and connections are stored.=
 Other Seesaw teams use the Secrets Manager as well.</p>
<p>To add a variable:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Add your variable name, value, description in <code>dart/airflow/terrafo=
rm/mwaa/prod/mwaa_variables.json</code> file present in dart repo. Maintain=
 the order</p></li>
<li>
<p>If variable is sensitive then use placeholder <code>&lt;REPLACE_ME&gt;</=
code> as value. Don=E2=80=99t put value directly in PR for such variables.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Before merging the changes in main branch, follow the <a class=3D"extern=
al-link" href=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/edi=
t-v2/88473854#Terraform-Process" rel=3D"nofollow">steps</a> to run terrafor=
m apply.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><br>
To add a connection:<br><br>
You may need permission to add secrets in order to do this. Ask in #prod-pl=
atform.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Go to Secrets Manager in the console: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D=
"https://us-west-2.console.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/listsecrets?region=
=3Dus-west-2" rel=3D"nofollow"><u>https://us-west-2.console.aws.amazon.com/=
secretsmanager/listsecrets?region=3Dus-west-2</u></a></p></li>
<li>
<p>Click =E2=80=9CStore a new secret=E2=80=9D and enter the name and value.=
 <strong>The secret name should follow the following convention:</strong></=
p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>It should begin with =E2=80=9CMWAA/=E2=80=9D. Otherwise MWAA may not hav=
e permission to access it.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Connections should then have =E2=80=9Cconnections/=E2=80=9D .</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p>For example, to add a connection called TEST_CONN, you would set the nam=
e to be =E2=80=9CMWAA/connections/TEST_CONN=E2=80=9D. See other MWAA secret=
s for examples.</p>
<p>For more information, see <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://doc=
s.aws.amazon.com/mwaa/latest/userguide/connections-secrets-manager.html#con=
nections-sm-createsecret-connection" rel=3D"nofollow"><u>this</u></a> for a=
dding connections.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_pgmg3rdg1pf6Local"><span class=3D"conflu=
ence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_pgmg3rdg1pf6"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_pgmg3rdg1pf6"></span></span>Local</h2>
<p>See <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/=
wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/88473854/Airflow+Development+Guide#%5BinlineExtension=
%5DAdd-Connection-and-Variables" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-colorid=3D"r7s=
1e7flzi"><u>setup steps above</u></span></a>.</p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_e1vles4rz5xtAdditionalDAGNotes"><span cl=
ass=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_e1vles4rz5xt"=
><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_e1vles4rz5xt"></span></span>=
<strong>Additional DAG Notes</strong></h1>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_3qmz9g8n8d3cCallbacks"><span class=3D"co=
nfluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_3qmz9g8n8d3c"><span cl=
ass=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_3qmz9g8n8d3c"></span></span>Callbacks=
</h2>
<p>Each DAG should have a success and failure callback. More info here: <a =
class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://docs.google.com/document/u/0/d/1M_1=
LmvLDrXKFKaBEdGmlkygFt9FmH89NLmWO_P5QElk/edit" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-=
colorid=3D"nurazqijb5"><u>Technical Documentation on Datadog callbacks on A=
irflow DAGs</u></span></a></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_3nsmq8a3e5nzTroubleshooting"><span class=
=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_3nsmq8a3e5nz"><s=
pan class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_3nsmq8a3e5nz"></span></span>Tro=
ubleshooting</h1>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>While running docker hello-world(2nd step from prerequisites) if it is f=
ailing with =E2=80=9C<em>permission denied while trying to connect to the D=
ocker daemon socket at unix:///var/run/docker.sock=E2=80=9D</em><br><em> </=
em>=E2=80=94 sudo chmod 666 /var/run/docker.sock</p></li>
<li>
<p>While building image(3rd step from get started) if it fails somewhere <e=
m>=E2=80=9Cchmod u+x /systemlibs.sh &amp;&amp; /systemlibs.sh=E2=80=9D</em>=
<br><em> </em>=E2=80=94 try to add <em>--network host</em> to mwaa-local-en=
v line 56<br><span data-colorid=3D"jc66qt7wbt">build_image() { docker build=
 --network host --rm --compress -t amazon/mwaa-local:$AIRFLOW_VERSION ./doc=
ker }</span></p></li>
<li>
<p>While starting airflow(4th step form get started) if it is failing with =
=E2=80=9C<em>permission denied while trying to connect to the Docker daemon=
 socket at unix:///var/run/docker.sock=E2=80=9D</em><br><em> </em>=E2=80=94=
 sudo chmod 666 /var/run/docker.sock</p></li>
<li>
<p>While starting airflow if postgres db-data is failing and exiting with =
=E2=80=9C<em>permission denied</em>=E2=80=9D, try <a class=3D"external-link=
" href=3D"https://github.com/aws/aws-mwaa-local-runner/issues/45" rel=3D"no=
follow"><span data-colorid=3D"brgmo52nnn"><u>https://github.com/aws/aws-mwa=
a-local-runner/issues/45</u></span></a></p></li>
<li>
<p>If Airflow can=E2=80=99t find something, you can enter the shell of the =
running container to debug. To do that:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Run docker ps and copy the container ID of the running MWAA container.</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Run docker exec -it &lt;container ID&gt; bash , substituting in the cont=
ainer ID copied from the previous step.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>If you get an error that says image not found, do =E2=80=9Cdocker login=
=E2=80=9D, run <code>./mwaa-local-env build-image</code></p></li>
</ol>
<p><br><strong>Comments:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The 1st and 3rd issue are the same but 1st is 1 time and 3rd maybe you w=
ill face every time when you try to start airflow after system off/on.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p>If you face any other issue try adding here with solution(if you have).<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_gutr4dr8fh23AirflowCLI"><span class=3D"c=
onfluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_gutr4dr8fh23"><span c=
lass=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_gutr4dr8fh23"></span></span>Airflow =
CLI</h1>
<p>Because we are using MWAA instead of standalone Airflow, the CLI works t=
hrough a wrapper script: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://github.=
com/shadowpuppet/dart/blob/main/airflow/scripts/airflow-cli.sh" rel=3D"nofo=
llow"><span data-colorid=3D"imngbi8zbh"><u>airflow/scripts/airflow-cli.sh</=
u></span></a>.</p>
<p></p>
<p>For example, to see a list of DAGs, change to airflow/scripts directory =
and run:</p>
<p><code>./airflow-cli.sh -c dags list --d</code></p>
<p>For full help: ./airflow-cli.sh =E2=80=93help</p>
<p>To see which commands you can run: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"ht=
tps://docs.aws.amazon.com/mwaa/latest/userguide/airflow-cli-command-referen=
ce.html#airflow-cli-commands" rel=3D"nofollow"><span data-colorid=3D"zzx1jv=
7a64"><u>https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mwaa/latest/userguide/airflow-cli-comm=
and-reference.html#airflow-cli-commands</u></span></a></p>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-LocalAirflowCLI">Local Airflow CLI</h2>
<p>To run CLI commands on your local runner, start the local runner and in =
a separate terminal use <code>mwaa-local-env cli</code>. For example, to se=
e a list of DAGs:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cd aws-=
mwaa-local-runner
./mwaa-local-env cli dags list</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-TerraformProcess">Terraform Process</h1>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Any changes in terraform code or any files on which any terraform block =
depends, you need to do terraform apply manually(currently).</p></li>
<li>
<p>It=E2=80=99s always good to do terraform plan before apply so that it wi=
ll point you what are the changes apply will going to do.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Terraform should only be applied from the <code>main</code> branch.</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-Stepstorunterraform">Steps to run terrafo=
rm</h2>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>go to <code>dart/airflow/terraform/mwaa/prod</code> directory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>aws configure sso</code></p></li>
<li>
<p><code>export AWS_PROFILE=3Dprofile_name</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>do <code>terraform plan</code> and verify the proposed change is expecte=
d</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>It will ask for sensitive variable values. As of July 2025, there are no=
ne (see <strong>NOTE</strong> below), so you can pass <code>{}</code> or ju=
st run <code>terraform plan -var=3D'sensitive_airflow_variables=3D{}'</code=
>.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>do <code>terraform apply</code></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Apply the same value above for sensitive_airflow_variables</p></li>
<li>
<p>If you encounter an AWS permission error when applying, we may need to a=
sk DevOps to apply it instead, like <span class=3D"confluence-jim-macro jir=
a-issue" data-jira-key=3D"SEC-471" data-client-id=3D"SINGLE_e237ef9d-8dd2-3=
4de-8588-bf3b81a18d6a_88473854_712020:3aa06253-1b05-42a2-b9b6-a95af2383e21"=
> <a href=3D"https://seesawhq.atlassian.net/browse/SEC-471" class=3D"jira-i=
ssue-key"><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-wait issue-placeholder"></span>S=
EC-471</a> - <span class=3D"summary">Getting issue details...</span> <span =
class=3D"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-default issue-placehold=
er">STATUS</span> </span> .</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p><br><strong>NOTE</strong>: <br>
We used pass 1 sensitive variable=E2=80=99s value through command line, <co=
de>AIRBYTE_API_KEY</code>. In such cases, the command looks like <code>terr=
aform plan -var=3D'sensitive_airflow_variables=3D{"AIRBYTE_API_KEY"=3D"take=
_value_from_aws_secrets_manager"}'</code></p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-Administration">Administration</h1>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_jgayw5m2gnkqHowtoupgradeAirflowversion">=
<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_jgayw=
5m2gnkq"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_jgayw5m2gnkq"></span=
></span><strong>How to upgrade Airflow version</strong></h2>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> because <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https:=
//github.com/shadowpuppet/aws-mwaa-local-runner" rel=3D"nofollow"><u>aws-mw=
aa-local-runner</u></a> is a forked public repo into our organization, it c=
an=E2=80=99t be made private. <strong>Do not push any account identifiers o=
r secrets to the repo in GitHub.</strong></p>
<p></p>
<p>Dart:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Change airflow_version under resource =E2=80=9Caws_mwaa_environment=E2=
=80=9D in terraform <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://main.tf" rel=
=3D"nofollow">main.tf</a></p></li>
<li>
<p>Change the dependency version in requirements.txt according to the const=
raints.</p></li>
<li>
<p>terraform plan - will show about updates</p></li>
<li>
<p>terraform apply(it may take time around 40-50 mins, don=E2=80=99t rememb=
er exact timing but it took lot of time during upgrade from 2.7.2 to 2.8.1)=
</p></li>
<li>
<p>Keep eye on webserver logs in cloudwatch. If everything goes fine, airfl=
ow will be upgraded successfully.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>mwaa forked repos:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>check new branch available with new version in aws-mwaa-local-runner ori=
ginal repo. Eg: v2.8.1</p></li>
<li>
<p>If new version available then do sync fork(you will find button) in our =
forked aws-mwaa-local-runner repo.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Update requirements.txt according to new constraints in forked repo.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>If we want to skip above 3 then follow <a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://github.com/aws/aws-mwaa-local-runner/pull/362" rel=3D"nofollow"=
><u>PR</u></a>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Update submodule in our dart repo on top of new changes(which has new ai=
rflow version) in forked repo.</p></li>
</ol>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-AirflowConnectiontoSnowflake">Airflow Con=
nection to Snowflake</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Production</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Airflow Connection Name: <code>snowflake_conn_serviceaccount</code></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Snowflake User: <code>SERVICE_ACCOUNT_AIRFLOW</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Snowflake Role: <code>AIRFLOW_SERVICE_ROLE</code></p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Dev</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>See <span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide=
-_7umb9rpuzd6j"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_7umb9rpuzd6j"=
></span></span> above</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>The Snowflake grants and settings for these roles are kept in <code>dart=
/tree/main/snowflake/roles/airflow.sql</code>. The main branch should be ke=
pt in sync with Snowflake.</p>
<h1 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_7iwsadehgdwiOtherInfo"><span class=3D"co=
nfluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_7iwsadehgdwi"><span cl=
ass=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_7iwsadehgdwi"></span></span>Other Inf=
o</h1>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_t76vdrizcrpkChangesdoneintheforkedrepo">=
<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_t76vd=
rizcrpk"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_t76vdrizcrpk"></span=
></span>Changes done in the forked repo</h2>
<p>These are the modifications we made to the AWS version of the test conta=
iner when this was first set up at Seesaw (<a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/browse/BEEH-16" rel=3D"nofollow"><span=
 data-colorid=3D"tz2s2y7hz1"><u>BEEH-16</u></span></a>):</p>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Updated aws access key, secret key, session token, region in docker/conf=
ig/.env.localrunner to read from local environment variable.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Updated secrets backend to localFileSystem in docker/config/airflow.cfg =
for connections and variables.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Added <em>--network host</em> to Mwaa-local-env line 56 because build-im=
age command was failing.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Updated requirements/requirements.txt with all the required dependencies=
</p></li>
<li>
<p>Connections can be defined as uri(string) or json(object) in connections=
.json.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Added line to copy new files to airflow_home in docker/Dockerfile</p></l=
i>
</ol>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-_xafunemg8ft3HowtoConnecttoDashboardRDSDa=
tabase"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuid=
e-_xafunemg8ft3"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"_xafunemg8ft3=
"></span></span>How to Connect to Dashboard RDS Database</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-CommandLine">Command Line</h3>
<p>This is how to connect to the test DB for the dashboard app, which is no=
t accessible to the public Internet and requires an SSH tunnel.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Requires:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>authentication to AWS via awscli</p></li>
<li>
<p>psql installed</p></li>
<li>
<p>external IP address added to SSH server allowlist (ask Core Platform to =
do this in #help-security)</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Download the pem file from 1Password. See step in <a class=3D"external-l=
ink" href=3D"https://seesaw-eng.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/8847385=
4/Airflow+Development+Guide#%5BinlineExtension%5DRDS-Postgres-Connection" r=
el=3D"nofollow">RDS Postgres Connection</a> setup above.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use the pem file to open the tunnel: <code>ssh -i "~/Downloads/rds_proxy=
_dev.pem" -L 5432:test-seesaw-db-proxy.proxy-ceu8xezttjlx.us-west-2.rds.ama=
zonaws.com:5432 ec2-user@ec2-52-40-44-6.us-west-2.compute.amazonaws.com -N =
-f</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Run these commands to get a password and connect, like below. For read/w=
rite, change user to <code>gcsqltestrwdataplatform</code> in passport and p=
sql steps.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">export =
PGPASSWORD=3D"$(aws rds generate-db-auth-token \
--hostname test-seesaw-db-proxy.proxy-ceu8xezttjlx.us-west-2.rds.amazonaws.=
com \
--port 5432 \
--region us-west-2 \
--username gcsqltestrodataplatform)"

export RDSHOST=3D"127.0.0.1"

psql "host=3D$RDSHOST port=3D5432 sslmode=3Drequire dbname=3Dseesaw user=3D=
gcsqltestrodataplatform"</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"AirflowDevelopmentGuide-AWSConsole">AWS Console</h3>
<p>You can also run simple queries in the <a class=3D"external-link" href=
=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/query-edit=
or.html#query-editor.running" rel=3D"nofollow">Query Editor</a> in the AWS =
console:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Database instance: <code>test-seesaw-db</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Username: =E2=80=9CConnect with a Secrets Manager ARN=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li>
<p>Secrets Manager ARN: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://start.1p=
assword.com/open/i?a=3D4ZV5CLLCVRBO3D6SLLKUNVQGGU&amp;v=3Dv4pt7m3kjkiz6sakt=
6mul27reu&amp;i=3Dxufmmkkelgx46yfq6rszwuu2dy&amp;h=3Dseesawhq.1password.com=
" rel=3D"nofollow">see "Data Dashboard test database info" in 1Password</a>=
</p></li>
<li>
<p>Database: <code>seesaw</code></p></li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
